F account"}, {"snippet": "8.33% to the Employees' Pension Scheme (EPS)"}], "reference_indexes": [2]}, {"snippet": "Wage Ceiling & Rules: Under recent updates (effective September 17, 2026), the statutory EPF wage ceiling is ₹25,000 per month (up from the previous ₹15,000 limit). Contributions on wages above the ceiling remain optional/voluntary unless agreed upon via a joint request.", "reference_indexes": [1, 3]}, {"snippet": "Lower Rate Exception: A reduced rate of 10% applies in specific instances, such as for establishments with fewer than 10 employees or certain sick/loss-making industries ."}], "reference_indexes": [4]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "Would you like to know how to calculate your monthly take-home salary using the updated ₹25,000 wage ceiling or explore Voluntary Provident Fund (VPF) options?"}], "references": [{"index": 0, "title": "EPF Contribution: Rates, Calculation & Compliance", "link": "https://www.intervue.io/glossary/epf-contribution", "snippet": "Frequently Asked Questions * What is the current EPF contribution rate for employers and employees? The current epf contribution rate is 12% of the employee's basi...", "source": "Intervue", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.intervue.io&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL"}, {"index": 1, "title": "New PF Deduction Rules 2026: ₹25,000 Ceiling & 50% Rule", "link": "https://sbshr.com/new-pf-deduction-rules-2026/", "snippet": "Table_title: PF basics: the rates have not changed Table_content: | Component | Paid by | Rate | | --- | --- | --- | | EPF (employee share) | Employee | 12% | | EP...", "source": "SBS HR", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://sbshr.com&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL", "thumbnail": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRqK1-9kRdbR7ArElBnMQibvmp6FSkphnFN36BWw0g_yTESZMX_nxJ36-M3GvNRHp3fa61iYGp2U25QFutSvfxGlxmnfxyLoumyFvZy"}, 